{
  "description": "Push to an iPhone/iPad without a session: K_push = HKDF-SHA256(PRK, empty salt, info \"handlive/v1/push\", L = 32); the envelope is built as over a session and encrypted with K_push exactly as 0.5.1 (payload = b64(nonce(24) ‖ ciphertext ‖ tag(16)), AAD = UTF-8 \"<v>|<type>|<id>|<ts>\"); env_b64 = standard base64 (with padding) of the UTF-8 envelope JSON, sent as env_b64 of POST /v1/push and as hl of the APNs payload. I-NSE derives K_push from the PRK of pair p, decodes hl, rebuilds the AAD from the parsed envelope and decrypts.",
